  "reviewNotes": [
    "PAT is a rapid categorical visual assessment, not a numeric additive score.",
    "The current recommendation explicitly lists seven pattern interpretations; the eighth possible binary pattern is not present in the text key and is intentionally left unmapped.",
    "The recommendation separately gives triage-level 1-5 disposition guidance, but the text page does not provide an explicit pattern-to-level mapping; MiniMed must not infer one.",
    "PAT is intended to identify urgency and syndrome pattern before detailed ABCDE/instrumental assessment; it does not replace the subsequent clinical examination.",
